  "abstract": "A strong entry of a rational Diophantine sextuple can be repeated while retaining all 21 square roots. We use the normalization torus of a degenerating induced elliptic curve to bound the Mordell–Weil ranks required to split the two entries. Exact certificates on 1,710 markings of 4,484 explicit sextuples give six-point ranks three through six. In 330 of 342 repeated-entry choices, an induced curve requires rank six. On one fixed-product cyclic anchor family, a trace obstruction rules out a section through a prescribed exterior orbit on the ordered genus-one base and on all unramified double covers with a rational marked lift. An explicit ramified double cover of genus three carries the orbit with its individual roots. A second trace obstruction rules out extending the complete marked list on this cover.",
